<title>USA: Central Newspapers to close paper, take Q1 charge.</title>
<headline>Central Newspapers to close paper, take Q1 charge.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Newspapers Inc said Monday it will close its Phoenix afternoon paper, The Phoenix Gazette, as of January 18, and reorganize its morning Arizona Republic, cutting about 85 jobs.</p>
<p>As a result of the planned actions, the company said it plans to take a one-time charge in the first quarter of 1997 of $4.2 to $4.8 million.</p>
<p>Excluding the special charge, the company said it expects pre-tax earnings will have a benefit of about $5 million in 1997 and an ongoing annual benefit of about $6.4 million.</p>
